# [UNOFFICIAL] H96 Max V58 · Armbian on RK3588 · open GPU stack · v4.0

> **Device:** H96 Max V58 (Rockchip RK3588, 8GB RAM, 64GB eMMC)
> **Status:** Unofficial, community built, not affiliated with the Armbian project

---

## What is this

A ready-to-flash Armbian image for the H96 Max V58 Android TV box, plus the board
sources that image is built from. The box stops being a locked-down Android player and
becomes an ordinary arm64 Linux machine.

The image boots headless with SSH on first power-on. You choose a desktop afterwards,
or you never install one and run it as a small always-on server.

The centrepiece is the GPU. This build does not use the closed vendor Mali blob. It runs
the open **Panthor** kernel driver with **Mesa**, so the desktop composites on the
Mali-G610 itself instead of falling back to software rendering, Vulkan functions Vulkan
(PanVK 1.4), and video decodes on the Rockchip VPU.

