## What you get

| Feature | Notes |
|---|---|
| Open GPU stack | Panthor DRM + Mesa (Panfrost). KDE and GNOME composite on the GPU, renderer reports `Mali-G610 MC4 (Panfrost)`, not `llvmpipe`. Hardware cursor plane. |
| Open Vulkan | PanVK 1.4 on the Mali-G610, no vendor blob. |
| Hardware video | Rockchip MPP through mpv, roughly 1.5% CPU on 1080p. The `ff2mpv` browser button hands the page's video to it. |
| WiFi 6 | The radio is **PCIe**, not SDIO, so it does not share pins with Ethernet and both run at the same time. Connect with `sudo h96-wifi-connect`, or the WiFi tray icon on the desktop. |
| Bluetooth | BCM4362A2 with the vendor firmware baked into the image and loaded at boot by `h96-bt.service`. A2DP audio out, with LDAC, aptX HD and aptX alongside SBC. |
| HDMI audio | The default output. S/PDIF optical stays selectable, and the two now appear as `HDMI Out` and `S/PDIF Optical` instead of two identical names. |
| Front-panel display | The 4-digit panel on the front of the box works: clock with a blinking colon, plus the Ethernet, WiFi, USB and play icons driven from live system state (`h96-vfd.service`). |
| Power profiles | Performance, Balanced and Power Saver move the CPU governors and the GPU frequency ceiling (1000 / 800 / 600 MHz) together, from the desktop power applet. |
| GPU monitoring | `nvtop`, Panthor aware, shipped in the image and usable over SSH. |
| NPU | 3 cores, ~6 TOPS. Driver `v0.9.8`, 1000 MHz, per-core load via `h96-npu`. The inference runtime is proprietary Rockchip software, so `h96-npu-setup` fetches it on demand rather than the image shipping it. |
| GPU upscaling | `h96-upscale` runs ravu-lite-ar-r4 as an mpv user shader on the Mali-G610, for about 10-13% more GPU time. Sharper than the built-in scalers, and unlike FSRCNNX or nnedi3 it fits this GPU's budget. Needs a desktop session. |
| Hardware video encode | H.264, HEVC and MJPEG on the VPU via `h96-encode`. 1080p measured faster than 180 fps. The bundled ffmpeg has no `libx264`, so this is the only encode path. |
| Gaming layer | box64 plus wine plus two DXVK builds, launched with `h96-game-mode`. Wine and DXVK are bundled in `/opt/h96-gaming`; box64 installs itself once the box first reaches the network. Nothing needs downloading. |
| IR receiver | Optional device-tree overlay; learn your own remote with `ir-keytable`. |
| SSH | On from the first boot. Default login `root` / `1234`. Change it. |

Once first-boot setup is finished, the system reaches multi-user in about 7 seconds.

