## Desktops

**None are installed by default.** Pick one after flashing:

```
armbian-config  ->  System  ->  Desktop
```

GNOME (GDM) and KDE Plasma (SDDM) configure themselves the moment the display manager
package lands: GPU environment, polkit agent, audio, Bluetooth, network applet and
printer module are all set up with no manual steps. X11 desktops such as XFCE work the
same way through LightDM.

KDE keeps installing packages in the background after you first reach the desktop, and
the screen can go blank with only a cursor partway through. Both are expected. Give it
ten minutes or more before deciding something is missing, and do not reboot or unplug
the box while it is installing.

