## Flashing

**You need:** a Linux host, `rkdeveloptool`, and a USB-A to USB-A cable (male at both ends).

```bash
# 1a. First flash, Maskrom mode:
#     power off, hold the pinhole on the underside, plug USB into the box's USB2 port, release
# 1b. Reflashing a box already running this image: SSH in and run
#     reboot loader

# 2. Confirm the host sees it
rkdeveloptool ld
#    expect: DevNo=1  Vid=0x2207,Pid=0x350b  Maskrom  (or Loader)

# 3. Write it
xz -d H96-MAX-V58_Unofficial-Armbian_v4.0.img.xz
rkdeveloptool wl 0 H96-MAX-V58_Unofficial-Armbian_v4.0.img
rkdeveloptool rd
```

Writing takes a few minutes. **Never interrupt `wl` once it starts.**

> **Ethernet on the first boot.** The first boot stages the open GPU stack and pulls a
> small number of packages, then reboots itself once. Plug the box into your network for
> that boot. Everything after it runs standalone.

```bash
ssh root@<ip>     # password: 1234
```

The release download ships a full flashing guide (`FLASHING.md`), a scripted flasher
(`flash.py`), and a reference for every command and service this build adds
(`COMMANDS.md`).

